@@ -3,3 +3,20 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` returns the JSON value identified by an
+[RFC 6901 JSON Pointer](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901). The empty
+pointer (`""`) refers to the whole document. Each `/`-separated token selects
+an object member or zero-based array element; within a token, encode `~` as
+`~0` and `/` as `~1`.
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from "json-toolkit";
+
+resolvePointer({ users: [{ name: "Ada" }] }, "/users/0/name"); // "Ada"
+```
+
+Invalid pointer syntax and pointers that refer to missing values throw an
+`Error`. A `-` token does not resolve an array element under RFC 6901.
